            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0600" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4543: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-03T13:00:00+01:00">March 3, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 3—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. A few minutes before the opening of the Assembly meeting Sato handed me the following message: <pb
                        facs="0601" n="497" xml:id="pg497"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In view of the retreat of the Chinese forces beyond 20 kilometers to the
                            north of Shanghai the Japanese troops stopped on a line situated at
                            about that distance. The Japanese troops will abstain from all acts of
                            hostilities except those of a strictly defensive nature and will take
                            all measures necessary to the security of inhabitants. The Japanese
                            commanders have made public a declaration to this effect (evening of
                            March 3rd local time).”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
